  "captions": {
    "C1": "Weak-grid small-signal stability of a converter exporting 1 pu versus short-circuit ratio. (a) Grid-following converter (SRF-PLL, 2 ms current loop, AC-voltage PI): real part of the dominant eigenvalue for PLL bandwidths 10, 20 and 40 Hz; shaded band = unstable; dashed line SCR = 3 (IEEE Std 1204 weak-grid threshold). Above SCR 2 the dominant pole is the slow real AC-voltage-integrator pole; below SCR 2 a coupled PLL/voltage-loop oscillatory pair (5 to 7 Hz) takes over and crosses into the RHP. (b) Grid-forming VSM (Xv = 0.15 pu, D = 20 pu): swing-mode damping ratio for H = 2 s and 5 s.",
    "C2": "Eigenvalue loci as SCR falls from 10 to the static limit (colour = SCR); modes faster than -200 1/s omitted. Left: GFL with 20 Hz PLL. Right: GFM with H = 5 s."
  }
